Repro: force-stop com.izzes.nears after switching to Food & Restaurant (module_switched fired, cache persisted); relaunch (adb shell am start). App correctly lands directly on Food & Restaurant home (no picker, last-used module honored) but no module_restored event fires anywhere in a clean adb logcat -c-scoped capture across the whole relaunch-to-home-ready window (only app_open + sectors_shown{sectors_count:3, zone_id:2} logged).

Root cause: UserApp/lib/helper/destination_resolver.dart's pre-existing DestinationTier.restoredModuleHome (NEARS-1551) — "multiple visible modules, but the cached prior selection is still one of them: splash restores that module silently" — routes through ModuleController.selectModuleNavFree() and explicitly does NOT fire sector_auto_selected NOR (unlike ModuleController.autoSelectDefaultModule, this ticket's own new function) module_restored. destination_resolver.disarmAutoSelect() is called for this tier before home's own ModuleController.consumeAutoSelectDefaultModule() gate gets a chance to run, so the NEW module_restored event this ticket added is structurally unreachable on the resolver's own fast "returning user" path — arguably the MOST COMMON real-world cold-open shape for a repeat user in a multi-module zone. This undermines the ticket's own "success metric" (module_restored vs module_switched share), which depends on module_restored firing on (near) every cold open to be meaningful.
